===== README.md (Scaffold) =====
# @acme/todos

A typed TypeScript client for the **Todos 1.2.3** RPC, generated by `leptoskit rpc generate --target typescript`.

It has no dependencies and uses the platform `fetch`; the calls go to the same routes the app itself uses. The package ships TypeScript source (`index.ts`), which Deno, Bun, and TypeScript-aware bundlers load directly; for plain Node, compile it with `npx tsc -p .`.

## Usage

```ts
import { Client, FnError } from "@acme/todos";

const api = new Client({ serverUrl: "https://todos.example" });

try {
	const result = await api.listTodos({ filter: /* ... */ });
} catch (error) {
	if (error instanceof FnError && error.retryable) {
		// a network or server failure: safe to try again
	}
	throw error;
}
```

`Client` takes `serverUrl` (defaults to the page's own origin), `headers` sent with every request (for example `Authorization`), and a `fetch` implementation.

Errors are `FnError` instances with a `kind` of `network`, `invalid`, `server`, `decode`, or `other`, mirroring the server's classification; `retryable` is true only for `network`.

## Live

Queries, mutations and channels also run over one WebSocket to the server's `/live`, opened on first use:

```ts
const stop = api.searchTodos.subscribe({ /* ... */ }, (value) => render(value));
await api.completeTodo.live({ /* ... */ });
const room = api.todoRoom.join({ /* ... */ }, { onSignal: (message, from) => show(message), onPresence: (members) => list(members) });
room.signal(/* ... */);
```

A subscription gets the first value and every change; lists of rows change by patch, so a long list costs about one row per update. `.live(...)` resolves once your own subscriptions show the write, or after `readYourWritesMs` (2 seconds by default) if none of them changes. The connection reconnects with backoff, subscribes again, and re-sends a mutation whose answer was lost with the same key, so it runs once. Sign in with `new Client({ live: { token: () => accessToken } })`; watch `api.live.onStatus(...)` for a connection banner, and call `api.live.close()` when done.
